IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Human Rights (Sexual Conduct) Act 1994 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, RULES AND
-- TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C2004A04852.txt
-- (compilation C2009C00395). Seat: the adult whose conduct is in question.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `Kind of law` IS ONE OF
    `a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory`
    `some other law`

DECLARE `Conduct` HAS
    `the date`                                          IS A DATE
    -- s 4(1): "involving only" these people
    `dates of birth of those involved`                  IS A LIST OF DATE
    `all consented`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `in private`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the interfering law`                               IS A `Kind of law`
    -- s 4(1): "arbitrary interference with privacy within the meaning of
    -- Article 17" — a finding
    `the interference is arbitrary`                     IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Sexual conduct position` HAS
    `everyone involved is an adult`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct is protected by s 4`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the interference is barred by s 4`                 IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

§ `Rules`

-- s 4(2): "an adult is a person who is 18 years old or more". A person is 18
-- on the eighteenth anniversary of birth (F1).
@ref s 4(2)
GIVEN b IS A DATE, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `born on` b `is an adult on` d IF
    `add months` b 216 AT MOST d

@ref s 4(1)-(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `everyone involved is an adult for` c IF
        NOT (c's `dates of birth of those involved` EQUALS EMPTY)
    AND all (GIVEN b YIELD `born on` b `is an adult on` (c's `the date`)) (c's `dates of birth of those involved`)

-- s 4(1): "Sexual conduct involving only consenting adults acting in
-- private".
@ref s 4(1)
@export Is my sexual conduct within s 4(1) of the Human Rights (Sexual Conduct) Act 1994 (Cth)? Yes if it involved only adults (18 or more), all consenting, acting in private. DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct`  @desc The date, the dates of birth of those involved, consent and privacy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is protected for` c IF
        `everyone involved is an adult for` c
    AND c's `all consented`
    AND c's `in private`

-- s 4(1): such conduct "is not to be subject, by or under any law of the
-- Commonwealth, a State or a Territory, to any arbitrary interference with
-- privacy". Conditional on the finding that the interference is arbitrary.
@ref s 4(1)
@export Does s 4(1) of the Human Rights (Sexual Conduct) Act 1994 (Cth) bar the interference with my conduct? Yes where the conduct is protected and the interference, under a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory, is arbitrary within the meaning of Article 17 of the ICCPR; no where it is not arbitrary, the conduct is not protected, or the interference is under any other law (which s 4 does not reach). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct`  @desc The conduct, the law under which it is interfered with, and whether the interference is arbitrary
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the interference is barred for` c MEANS
    IF c's `the interfering law` EQUALS `some other law`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST (`the conduct is protected for` c AND c's `the interference is arbitrary`)

§ `The top-level goal`

@ref ss 3-4
@export default The position under the Human Rights (Sexual Conduct) Act 1994 (Cth) of an adult whose private sexual conduct is in question: whether everyone involved is an adult, whether the conduct is protected by s 4(1), and whether an interference under a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory is barred (where it is arbitrary within Article 17 of the ICCPR). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct`  @desc The conduct and the interference
GIVETH A `Sexual conduct position`
`the sexual conduct position for` c MEANS
    `Sexual conduct position` WITH
        `everyone involved is an adult`                 IS `everyone involved is an adult for` c
        `the conduct is protected by s 4`               IS `the conduct is protected for` c
        `the interference is barred by s 4`             IS `the interference is barred for` c
